# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# @astrojs/sitemap writes /sitemap-index.xml, and robots.txt points there, so
# Google already finds it. But /sitemap.xml is the conventional path many
# crawlers and SEO tools probe first, and it was a 404 (checked live 5 Oct
# 2026). A permanent redirect sends them to the real index without a second
# copy of the file to keep in sync.
/sitemap.xml /sitemap-index.xml 301
